2:The HeritAge - Revenge of the forgotten prince|v1.20|created by [$800080]Thunder[Beer][HU][]||Speciel thanks for the Translators and for the Alpha Testers and all of those who gave feedbacks!|Dutch by [$00F0FF][Beer]Mithrellas[];|Polish by [$CC0030]sado[];|Russian by [$000000]Ritter_des_Todes[]|Grammatical assistance by [$CC0030]sado[] & DontTalk;||Have fun,|t
10:'Tarian the traitor organised and killed the king at New Years Eve. You, little prince, were knocked out by the loyal guards, who carried you over to the Northern-West province to a safe place. It is a great opportunity to learn here. Also, it's a fairly safe place, as long as you're known only by a couple of villagers. You have to work hard to get back what is rightfully yours..'
11:Unfortunately, the promised townhall was almost empty - it seems it was discovered by Tarian's groups, who emptied it... After the years you spent on the great plains, now Tarian knows he can't chase you anymore, and he is happy he could take hands on that secret gold. He moved his forces back to a castle close to the mid-west crossroads. The roads are important to control the region, as they're on the way to the capital of west. 
12:Now that the roads are not blocked anymore, we finally reached the Eastmost Wall of the kingdom. Rumor says Tarian's mercenaries left the area, so there's not many quality units defending the fortress. You need to take over the control of this wall. There is a lake nearby, which offers great supplies for the future.
13:If, after conquering the Impossible Fortress, you believed there is not much more to do here on the east, you were mistaken. There's still a town, which does not accept your claim to the throne. You need to persuade them to change their mindset...
14:Now that the Diamond Village is not shining anymore, you could shift your focus to the center of the kingdom. As always, there is a 'but'... before, you need to help out your strange cousin on the southern shore. She tries to prepare for the cold winter, but her efforts are being thwarted by the bandits. Take care of the Bones Island. It's called this way for a reason...
15:As a token of gratitude, your cousin gave you a map, leading to a little island, which would be a perfect camp to coordinate an invasion against Tarian's fully evolved empire from. Anything you should know? Well, the island is inhabited...
16:After getting a solid position on the island, now you can the focus on the middle area of the Kingdom. You are years late, so Tarian and his allies were able to fortify the major villages. Walls, and quality ones... Expect a longer campaign. Luckily, the shore is filled with gold, and your ally, Akacius, will support you from time to time, as much as he is able to.
17:After taking over the centre of the Kingdom, now you've opened an opportunity to move to Traian's birth place. It is a vast land and since Tarian got the crown, he invested the most of his resources into this area. A small river goes through the southwestern border, close to the great plains. The river blockes area, which could be used to build out your settlement. Leave your mark on this fancy land, to make Tarian as mad as possible.
18:One step away from the castle. This island has a lighthouse, perfect for executing the next part of your plan..
19:Your home's inches away. Now that the lights are off, everything is prepared for the grand entrance. Calm down, take a deep breath and feel the power of silence. It won't last for long.
